  "step_3": "The decision reason focuses on the maximum outcome of each lottery and prefers the one with the higher (more favorable) maximum. The maximum outcome of B (6000 Euros) is clearly higher than that of A (0 Euros), so the reason would select B. The individual’s reasoning also hinges on the fact that A offers nothing to win—i.e., its maximum is zero—while B offers a positive outcome. Although the individual does not explicitly use the phrase 'maximum outcome,' the reasoning aligns with comparing the best possible results of each lottery. The justification 'nothing to win in A' directly contrasts with the presence of a gain in B, which corresponds to the core logic of the decision reason. Therefore, the information considered and the justification match the decision rule closely. There is strong evidence that the individual used the maximum outcome as a decisive criterion.",
  "final_assessment_score": 95
